<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Adapted from FOPP "Printing Intermediate Results". GNU FDL 1.3; see ch-loops.ptx. -->
<section xml:id="sec-wp-printing">
  <title>&#x1F469;&#x200D;&#x1F4BB; Printing Intermediate Results</title>

  <p>
    A loop does a lot of work where you cannot see it.
    When the answer at the end is wrong, you need a way to look inside.
    The simplest way is to add <c>console.log</c> lines in the loop body,
    so the loop tells you what it is doing on every pass.
  </p>

  <p>
    This program is supposed to add up the numbers in the array, but the answer is wrong.
  </p>

  <activity xml:id="try-wpprint-1">
    <title>A Buggy Total</title>
    <program xml:id="ac-wpprint-1" interactive="activecode" language="javascript">
    <code>
let nums = [5, 10, 15, 20];
let total = 0;

for (let i = 1; i &lt; nums.length; i++) {
  total = total + nums[i];
}

console.log(total);
    </code>
  </program>
  </activity>

  <p>
    Add a line to show <c>i</c> and the element on each pass:
  </p>

  <activity xml:id="try-wpprint-2">
    <title>Printing Inside the Loop</title>
    <program xml:id="ac-wpprint-2" interactive="activecode" language="javascript">
    <code>
let nums = [5, 10, 15, 20];
let total = 0;

for (let i = 1; i &lt; nums.length; i++) {
  console.log("i is " + i + ", nums[i] is " + nums[i]);
  total = total + nums[i];
}

console.log(total);
    </code>
  </program>
  </activity>

  <p>
    Now the bug is easy to see: the first line printed says <c>i is 1</c>.
    The loop never visited index 0, so the 5 was never added.
    Change the start to <c>let i = 0</c> and run it again.
  </p>

  <p>
    You can print as much as you need, and add labels so you can tell the lines apart:
  </p>

  <activity xml:id="try-wpprint-3">
    <title>Labeled Output</title>
    <program xml:id="ac-wpprint-3" interactive="activecode" language="javascript">
    <code>
let nums = [5, 10, 15, 20];
let total = 0;

console.log("***** before the loop *****");
for (let i = 0; i &lt; nums.length; i++) {
  console.log("--- pass with i = " + i + " ---");
  console.log("adding " + nums[i]);
  total = total + nums[i];
  console.log("total is now " + total);
}
console.log("***** after the loop *****");
console.log("final total: " + total);
    </code>
  </program>
  </activity>

  <p>
    Once the program works, take the extra <c>console.log</c> lines back out.
    They were there to help you, not to be part of the answer.
  </p>
</section>
